<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slave Abolition Act (Siam)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Slave Abolition Act of 1905 was the Siamese law that completed the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> begun by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chulalongkorn">Chulalongkorn</a> in 1874. It forbade any new enslavement and freed the children of slaves, while the remaining debt slaves had their redemption price reduced each month until they were free. The reform supplied free labour and taxpayers for the new centralised state.</p></div>
